{"config":{"lang":["en","hu"],"separator":"[\\s\\-]+","pipeline":["stopWordFilter"],"fields":{"title":{"boost":1000.0},"text":{"boost":1.0},"tags":{"boost":1000000.0}}},"docs":[{"location":"","title":"Charted","text":"<p>Charted is a self-hosted social hiking app: plan hiking routes, record and share hikes, follow other hikers, all in one place. This site is the web version of my BSc thesis written about it.</p>"},{"location":"#abstract","title":"Abstract","text":"<p>TODO</p>"},{"location":"#whats-inside","title":"What's inside","text":"<ul> <li> <p> Introduction</p> <p>The app, the goals and scope of the thesis, and the technologies used.</p> <p> Read the introduction</p> </li> <li> <p> User guide</p> <p>How to use the app, from registration through route planning and recording to the social features.</p> <p> Read the user guide</p> </li> <li> <p> Developer guide</p> <p>Design, system architecture, backend, mobile app, operations and test cases.</p> <p> Read the developer guide</p> </li> <li> <p> Summary</p> <p>Challenges and solutions, and the opportunities for a V2.</p> <p> Read the summary</p> </li> </ul>"},{"location":"#technologies","title":"Technologies","text":"<ul> <li>Mobile: React Native, Expo, MapLibre</li> <li>Backend: NestJS BFF, PostgreSQL, PostGIS, TypeORM</li> <li>Maps and routing: Valhalla, Martin</li> <li>Authentication: Keycloak (OAuth2, PKCE)</li> <li>Infrastructure: Docker Compose, Drone CI, two Raspberry Pis</li> </ul>"},{"location":"developer-guide/architectural-decisions/","title":"Architectural decisions","text":"<p>TODO</p>"},{"location":"developer-guide/","title":"Developer guide","text":"<p>TODO</p>"},{"location":"developer-guide/architecture/backend-and-bff/","title":"Backend and BFF architecture","text":"<p>TODO</p>"},{"location":"developer-guide/architecture/","title":"System architecture","text":"<p>TODO</p>"},{"location":"developer-guide/architecture/infrastructure/","title":"Infrastructure","text":"<p>TODO</p>"},{"location":"develo